+**Board resolution prerequisite for `--apply`:** `normalize-board` (both
+dry-run and `--apply`) resolves a board the same way every other command
+does — it requires the board dir to contain `board.jsonl` (the header)
+AND `events.jsonl` (even if empty). A tasks.jsonl-only board or a board
+with only `board.jsonl` fails with:
+
+```
+exit 2: no JSONL foreman board found: ... (a tasks.jsonl-only board:
+events.jsonl is missing)
+```
+
+If you are repairing a legacy board that still uses topology B (header on
+line 1 of tasks.jsonl, no `board.jsonl`), create an empty
+`events.jsonl` first — it is the file the resolver checks to confirm the
+board directory is a complete board, not a partial checkout.
+
 ```bash
 boardctl -C ~/myproject normalize-board               # classify + stage, zero board writes
 boardctl -C ~/myproject normalize-board --json        # machine-readable census
